{"strongs": "H7324", "word": "רִיק", "translit": "ruq", "root": "ריק", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb Hiph`il", "gloss": "make empty, empty out", "definition": "[ רִיק ] verb Hiph`il make empty, empty out (Arabic ( ) pour out, forth , intransitive (of water, blood, etc.); Aramaic רִיק empty, pour , in derivatives; Assyrian rê‡u , empty ); — Perfect 1 singular הֲרִי֫קֹתִי Lev 26:33 ; Mal 3:10 3 plural חֵרִיקוּ Ezek 28:7 ; Ezek 30:11 Imperfect 3 masculine singular יָרִיק Hab 1:17 , וַיָּ֫רֶק Gen 14:14 (but see below); Imperative masculine singular הָרֵק Ps 35:8 Infinitive construct הָרִיק Isa 32:6 Participle plural מְרִיקִים Gen 42:35 ; Zech 4:12 — 1. empty vessels Gen 42:35 ( E ) Jer 48:12 keep empty , לְחֶרִיק נֶפֶשׁ רָעֵב Isa 32:6 (i.e. keep hungry). 2. pour out or down , rain Mal 3:10 ; Eccl 11:3 , oil Zech 4:12 . 3. empty out (i.e. draw ) sword (compare Assyrian kakkê ittabbaku [passive], Dl HWB 699 b ) Exod 15:9 (poem), Lev 26:33 ( H ), Ezek 5:2 ; Ezek 5:12 ; Ezek 12:14 ; Ezek 28:7 ; Ezek 30:11 probably also Hab 1:17 ( חרבו for חרמוֺ Gie We Now ); of lance Ps 35:3 compare (several.) וירק חניכיו Gen 14:14 ( R ) led forth , < Samaritan וַיָּ֫דֶק (Aramaic דּוּק Aph`el look ) i.e. mustered ᵐ5 compare Di and others, ויפקּד Ball. — In Ps 18:43 ᵐ5 ᵑ6 Hup-Now Bae read אֲדִקֵּם ; so || 2Sam 22:43 MT; but De Dr < אֲרִיקֵם (see דקק ). Hoph`al be emptied out from vessel : Perfect 3 masculine singular הוּרק Jer 48:11 Imperfect 2 masculine singular תּוּרַק Song 1:3 (al. 3 feminine singular; of ointment, in simile); compare also Amos 6:6 , where Oort מוּרְקֵּי for מִזְרְקֵי .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7912')\">BDB7912</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H7324')\">H7324</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7911')\">BDB7911</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7913')\">BDB7913</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>רִיק</bdbheb>] <b>verb Hiph`il</b> <highlightword>make empty, empty out</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder5061/